# keur quality control — sonar-project.properties without sonar.organization.
#
# Why this exists: SonarCloud (the SaaS, sonarcloud.io) requires
# sonar.organization in addition to sonar.projectKey; without it the scanner
# cannot resolve the project and the analysis fails or mis-lands. Self-hosted
# SonarQube does NOT need it, so this is a warn, not a block (a SonarQube-only
# repo legitimately omits it). Nothing else validates the file, so an early
# nudge is the only signal that a SonarCloud setup is incomplete.
#
# HOW (absence engine): fires when NO line declares `sonar.organization`.
# Pre-filtered to the sonar property file by exact name + a cheap `sonar`
# content gate.
#
# WARN with low confidence: deliberately soft because SonarQube-only repos are a
# valid case; the fix text spells out when it applies. @see docs/rules-authoring.md
id: SONAR-002
ilities: [traceability]
maturity: 3
title: sonar-project.properties missing sonar.organization (SonarCloud)
category: quality
severity: warning
engine: absence
action: warn
confidence: 0.5
target:
  filenames: sonar-project.properties
  content_contains: sonar
patterns:
  - regex: (?m)^\s*sonar\.organization\s*=\s*\S
    message: "sonar-project.properties has no sonar.organization — SonarCloud requires it (self-hosted SonarQube does not). If this project targets sonarcloud.io, the scan will not resolve the project."
fix: "For SonarCloud, add `sonar.organization=<your-org-key>`. For self-hosted SonarQube only, this key is not needed and the warning can be suppressed with `keur:ignore SONAR-002`."
